v0.14.0b
------
Fixed a SimpleFIN sync bug that could import zero transactions every single sync for certain accounts
(brokerage/investment accounts especially): the bridge reports a transaction's `posted` field as 0 for
anything that hasn't posted yet, which was being treated as a missing/bad date and silently dropped
instead of imported as pending. Related fix: an account's very first sync now auto-corrects its starting
balance (bank-reported balance minus the transactions just imported) so the register's running balance
matches the real balance right away instead of coming up short by whatever activity fell outside the
90-day backfill window — only applies to a freshly-linked account with no prior history, never one you
were already using manually. The Bank Sync page's "Manage accounts" list now has an Unlink button on
each linked account, opening a choice of unlinking only, unlinking and closing the account, or
unlinking-close-and-permanently-delete in one click (closes and force-deletes automatically if it still
has transaction history, behind one confirmation warning it removes every transaction and schedule tied
to the account, not just the account record). Linking a remote account to a brand-new local account also
now offers a custom name instead of only the bank's own label.

v0.13.0b
------
Accounts can now be organized into custom groups (Accounts page: assign a group when adding/editing an
account, or create one on the fly with "+ New group"), shown as collapsible sections you can expand or
minimize — collapse state is remembered per browser. The Accounts table also gained a live filter row
under its column headers (name, type, balance, on budget), same pattern as the register's own filters.
Fixed: SimpleFIN bank sync could skip the 90-day backfill for a newly-linked account under a connection
that had already synced before, silently importing nothing until a transaction happened to post within
the short 7-day overlap window. Fixed: the account-delete confirmation could stay disabled forever for
an account named from a bank feed (e.g. a synced account whose name has a non-breaking space) since the
exact-match check couldn't be satisfied by typing a normal space. Also: the quick-add row's tiny "new
category group" dropdown is gone — a category typed there that doesn't exist yet is created in your
first category group automatically; use the full entry form to pick a different one. The bank sync
page's "linked accounts" column now lists one account per line instead of packing them into a single
comma-separated run. The top nav is now a hamburger menu (tap the icon next to the theme toggle) on
every screen size, matching Scored Waypoints' — it also gained a "Sync All" action (shown only once
you have at least one SimpleFIN bank connection) that syncs every connection in one go, and each
bank-linked account's register now has its own "Sync Now" button next to Import.

v0.12.1b
------
Fixed installing the Waypoints Portal alongside this app never making the portal reachable by FQDN or
a dedicated LAN-IP port — it only ever came up on its raw Docker-published port (plain HTTP). The
portal now also gets a host nginx site of its own (https://<portal-fqdn>/ plus LAN-IP port 8510 by
default) whenever one's available, added or repaired every time the portal is installed or linked to.

v0.12.0b
------
Every Docker-managed volume (logs, and MongoDB's data directory when using the bundled internal
container) can now be redirected to a host path instead of the managed Docker volume, via new
LOGS_HOST_DIR/MONGO_HOST_DIR vars in .env — same pattern as the existing BACKUP_HOST_DIR/SSL_CERT_FILE/
SSL_KEY_FILE. Leave blank to keep using the managed volume (the default — no change needed for existing
installs). Also fixed: the minimal-footprint install path wasn't honoring BACKUP_HOST_DIR in its
generated docker-compose.yml — it now does, matching the full-checkout path.

v0.11.1b
------
Linking this app's login to the Waypoints Portal (checked during setup) now fully automates SSO — it
registers this app as an OIDC client of the portal (headless, via the portal's own container) and
writes the OIDC_* fields into this app's own .env automatically, recreating the container to pick them
up. Previously this last step needed a manual visit to the portal's Admin > SSO clients.

v0.11.0b
------
Setup wizard: no longer offers a "Full checkout" footprint choice (always trims to the minimal
Docker-only footprint on a scratch install); fixed Docker auto-install failing on Rocky Linux;
install.sh now checks for Docker up front instead of failing deep into setup; MongoDB now defaults to
"External" (a shared instance) instead of bundling its own container; "Add an nginx site" is now
checked by default when a host nginx is detected; the host nginx direct-IP-access port default moved
from 8443 to 8511 (every Waypoints app now has its own, since a shared host nginx can't have two apps
on the same port — see PORTS.md in the portal repo); setup now offers to install the Waypoints Portal
(shared login across the family) non-interactively alongside its own setup, detecting an existing one
first so two never end up installed on one host

